              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Über die Composition der quadratischen Formen von beliebig vielen Variabeln
          %p
            The alternative classification as real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/alternative+algebra"} alternative
            division algebras is due to
          %ul
            %li#Zorn30
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Zorn"}> Max Zorn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Theorie der alternativen Ringe
          %p General discussion includes includes
          %ul
            %li#Tornheim52
              %p
                Leonard Tornheim,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Normed fields over the real and complex fields
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.mmj/1028989727"} Euclid
            %li
              %p
                Silvio Aurora,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On normed rings with monotone multiplication
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.pjm/1102977236"} JSTOR
          %p The result about removing the assumption of finite-dimensionality from unital normed division algebras appears in:
          %ul
            %li#UrbanikWright60
              Kazimierz Urbanik and Fred B. Wright,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Absolute-valued algebras
              %strong 11
              (1960), 861-866, doi:
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9939-1960-0120264-6"} 10.1090/S0002-9939-1960-0120264-6
          %p
            Exposition with emphasis on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/octonions/node2.html"} Normed Division Algebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/week59.html"} This Week’s Finds — Week 59
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+holonomy"} special holonomy
            modeled on the different normed division algebras is in
          %ul
            %li#Leung02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Naichung+Conan+Leung"}> Naichung Conan Leung
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Riemannian Geometry Over Different Normed Division Algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1090351387"} euclid
        .revisedby
